    "reply": "I added `tests/test_payments.py` with 11 tests, and `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes. I didn't change anything under `shop/`.\n\nThe tests cover three areas:\n- **`line_total`:** normal, zero-quantity and fractional-price cases.\n- **`order_total`:**\n  - An empty order totals 0.\n  - A single line includes tax.\n  - Several lines are summed before tax is applied.\n  - The result is rounded to two decimals.\n  - Changing `TAX_RATE` changes the total.\n- **`refund`:** partial, full and zero refunds.\n\n`refund` does no validation. A refund larger than the order total returns a negative number, and so does a negative refund amount. The function has no documented contract, so I didn't write a test that assumes a particular behavior. If you want it to reject those cases, tell me and I'll add `expectedFailure` tests for them.",
